A||||15||Cooter||Credit card number security.||||1||
Z||000000||Cooter||08-10-2001||12:08 AM||||I just had to call my card's company and shut the account down because someone has been making charges for me. The bad thing is that I almost did not catch it because the charges were in line with what I usually buy. I guess that I am trying to tell everyone to open your statement as soon as you get it and make sure the charges are really yours, no matter how small they seem to be because the ones on my card were really starting to add up.||||reg||1
Z||000001||thomas_l||08-10-2001||09:03 AM||||I agree - I have had two in the last year. The first one was some bogus $10 charge from a Russian company. My card co said they had a lot of activity on that one and they removed it immediately. The last one was a one way ticket on an airline I never use from a city I never visit. And the luser didn't even use the ticket according to the airline. Got that one removed too. I check each statement carefully and even monitor my most active accounts online periodically.<P>The latest (although not necessarily newest) thing around here has been clerks at stores grabbing the numbers by printing duplicate receipts and then going shopping on your behalf. There was a big bust at one of the big mall stores nearby where a bunch of people were arrested for that. The strategy is to make many small purchases on many different accounts that most folks would overlook. It's gotten so popular that one Bozo got arrested at a license check because the cop looked in the cab of this guys truck and he had piles of stolen mail and snatched credit cards and checks laying out in plain view!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||08-10-2001||09:56 AM||||Good advice guys. Thanks!<P>Thomas, Where has all of this been happening? Town Center? I haven't heard anything about it on the news for a long time.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000003||thomas_l||08-10-2001||11:13 AM||||North Point Mall. I think it was in the Lord & Taylor, but all those stores recruit out of the same labor pool. I just remember seeing it in the local newspaper a while ago. For that reason I tend to use store cards in those few mall stores I shop... at least the bad people won't F*** up one of my good cards.<P>The people that really get screwed are the folks that use debit cards a lot. Since it's a "cash" transaction the money is "gone" lone before you know it's happening. And the banks are really reluctant to help out.||||reg||1
Z||000004||SteveJ||08-10-2001||03:52 PM||||I had repeated $19.99 charges on mine from all over the place. Different computer sounding names as companies. Visa was good about canceling them although for the first couple I had to go through the 60 day waiting period for the "merchant" to reply. They never did.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||08-11-2001||10:06 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by thomas_l:<BR><B>...The people that really get screwed are the folks that use debit cards a lot. Since it's a "cash" transaction the money is "gone" lone before you know it's happening. And the banks are really reluctant to help out.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It's for this reason that I NEVER use debit cards. <BR>And the people at the bank almost sound like their feelings are hurt when I tell them I don't want a debit card OR an ATM card.<P><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Stage-2GT||08-11-2001||10:34 AM||||  There is a simple solution, well maybe not so simple, to this whole mess. Stop using credit cards. I have none, need none and don't want one. Credit cards are the government and big business way of keeping you down. They enslave you!! I have been debt free (except my house and my Suburban) for a good while and find it rather nice not having to worry about which card I am going to use to pay which card. <BR>  I know some will say you have to be responsible with your charges; that's a crock of doo-doo. Charging something is an open admission to the fact that you either can't afford it in the first place or, you don't care about putting a strain on your economy. Credit cards are responsible for 80% of all bankruptcies. Once you get in, you can't get out. Well, you can, but it's a load of work and trouble. Then, once your out, most jump right back in to achieve that life style they can't truly afford. <BR>  Sorry, didn't mean to make anyone mad, just my 2!<P>S2GT <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>------------------<BR>"If Hate Was Money, I Would Own The World"||||reg||8
Z||000007||annieL||08-11-2001||05:06 PM||||Years ago I needed to rent a car and the company I rented it from kept putting my debit card through. They did it about 5 times. It overdrew my checking account! I called and raised some stink about it because not only did they overdraw my account but the bank charged me a $30.00 overdraft fee. They had to charge back my debit card and the bank withdrew their fee but it was a nightmare!!||||reg||13
Z||000008||fiero56||08-11-2001||07:29 PM||||I have one credit card, and use it only when I am ordering stuff. That way I can fight the charges if I never see the items or they are $hit to begin with. Visa hasn't made a dime off of me. Other than my student loan($2K and falling), I am debt free. Bills are annoying enough without having to worry about debts/loans.<P>I have a friend who had their debit card number stolen twice in one year. We figure restaraunt employees snagged the numbers, but have no idea which restrnt did it. BTW, the bank never restored the lost money.||||reg||1
Z||000009||AusFiero||08-13-2001||10:09 AM||||You know what makes it worse. Credit card companies charge the user ridiculous interest charges to use the card. Then also charge the person providing the service or goods a percentage charge of each transaction. Talk about double dipping.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000010||Oreif||08-13-2001||11:13 AM||||We only use our debit/ATM card at the bank machine. (Can't stand using the others that charge a fee!!) Our credit card is an American Express Corporate card thru my work.<BR>No intrest and I see all that is on the bill every month. AE is very good about watching the account too. When I bought some stuff for the Fiero, the charge was over $250 and thru the internet. They called to verify it was me who placed the order. They said a flag goes up if it's over $250 or more than 3 purchases in 1 hour. Never had a problem yet.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Raydar||08-13-2001||04:57 PM||||I have three credit cards. A Visa that I use for personal stuff, A Discover that I (and my wife) use for "house" stuff and (usually) when we go out to eat, and an AMEX as a backup.<BR>We never charge more than we can pay for at the end of the month. Not at the obscene interest rates they charge. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000012||olympic||08-14-2001||12:49 AM||||I have about $30k in credit cards @ 27 years old.  A visa, M/C and AE for personal use(don't know why I have the last 2 I never use them), 1 visa for my business.  Both visa's charge less than 10% interest so it's cheaper than going to the bank for a loan.  I've bought cars, furniture, everything on them.  I know what I can safely spend(and pay back) but many of my frinds have gotten in way over their heads and it's almost impossible to get out.<P>Here's a little tip that not many people know.  Call your card company and ask for their "low intrerest option".  I pay a $25/year fee on my visa's and that lowers my interest from ~20% to down under 10%.  They don't advertise this option so you have to ask.||||reg||1
Z||000013||thomas_l||08-14-2001||01:09 PM||||Never heard of a low interest "option" - maybe that's a Canadian thing. I have a Visa that is used for short-term "loans" that is fixed 10.9%. My credit union can't even beat that with a loan. If you use cards at all it pays to shop them every few months, especially if you are working on improving a rickety credit history. Almost everything else I buy goes across a SkyMiles AMEX. A year of that got my wife and I to Calgary last month on reward tickets (+/- $1200 value depending on the going fares). The best place to shop rates is bankrate.com - choose low interest, perks, whatever fits your spending and bill paying habits.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Cooter||08-14-2001||11:37 PM||||One of the charges was to Earthlink's internet service. Who ever it was used a first/last name as their Earthlink screen name. I looked in the phone book and he lives about 3 blocks away from me! How can I prove to the authorities that he stole my CC information?||||reg||8
Z||000015||DecadenceR||08-14-2001||11:54 PM||||My dad just fopund out that someone was charging porn sites online to his checking account. <BR>First words ot of my mouth were "wasn't me...", cause I seem to get blamed for almost anything that happens here.||||reg||1
